            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0735" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/4–348: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sebald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-03">April 3,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received April 8—9:51 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–66. For the Department’s information, there follows the text of a press release
                    issued by the Public Information Office, General Headquarters, Far East Command
                    on April 1, 1948: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Brig. Gen. Courtney Whitney, Chief of SCAP’s Government Section, has
                            pointed out that the purge program, while fully consistent <pb
                                facs="0736" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/> with the purposes of the
                            Japanese Government and people in charting a democratic future, is one
                            of the direct requirements of the Potsdam Declaration. As such, final
                            action taken thereunder is regarded to be of a permanent nature for
                            which the Allied powers will unquestionably hold future Japanese
                            governments fully responsible.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sebald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
